// #2276 review round 13: the map-key walk has to terminate on a CYCLIC alias
// chain on its own. The depth cap used to do that; the visited set does it
// now, and this pins that the walk still halts -- a regression here hangs the
// compiler rather than failing.
// #3536: the cycle itself is refused now (an alias is expanded in place, so
// `A` names no type), so the row expects that refusal. The walk over `M`
// still runs on the completed declarations, so a hang still fails the row.
type A[T] = B[T]
type B[T] = A[T]

type M[T] = Map[A[T], Int]

fn f(m: M[String]) -> Int {
  0
}

fn main {
  ()
}
